#command

# Vim-style navigation for less.
#
# Most vim motions already work in less by default and need no binding:
#   j / k         line down / up
#   ^F / ^B       page forward / back
#   ^D / ^U       half-page down / up   (also d / u)
#   g / G         top / bottom          (typing gg also lands on top)
#   / n N         search, next, prev
#   ^E / ^Y       scroll one line down / up
#
# The only real gap is horizontal motion: by default h is the help screen
# and l is unbound. Rebind them to vim-style horizontal scroll (handy since
# we run less with -S, which chops rather than wraps long lines).
h  left-scroll
l  right-scroll

# h used to open the help screen; keep help reachable on H.
H  help

# Mirror the Swedish-keyboard motions from the vim config (ö = line start,
# ä = line end). A pager has no in-line cursor, so map them to the horizontal
# extremes: ö jumps back to the first column, ä to the end of the longest line.
ö  no-scroll
ä  end-scroll

# Clear search highlighting, mirroring the vim ,<cr> -> :noh mapping.
# (, becomes a prefix key; Enter alone still scrolls one line forward.)
,\r  undo-hilite
,\n  undo-hilite

# Cycle between files like vim tabs. Only relevant when several files are
# opened at once, e.g. `less a b c`. Tab -> next, Shift-Tab -> previous.
\t   next-file
\kt  prev-file
